<p>I think there's an SCP that's literally the <em>Book of the Dead</em>, but I don't recall quite how that one goes. Also CWW/Scanny's Egyptian sword/khopesh that has to do with the Ancient Egyptians believing that the heart controlled the body? And the temple that I think builds itself? Those are the ones that come to mind for me immediately. There's probably several more at least&#8212;Egyptian mythology is absolutely fascinating. (<sub>when i was in 6th grade one time my class went on a field trip to a small museum that ran CAT scans on mummies and the museum guide and i had a nice chat about the artifacts and random lore/mythology trivia and it was great</sub>)</p>
<p>Regarding the vocalizations&#8212;most of the &quot;spells&quot; are direct translations from the Wikipedia article on the spells from the <em>Book of the Dead</em>. There's some rather intriguing stuff mentioned in there regarding names to speak and the right things to say.</p>
<p>Thanks for the +1!</p>
<p>ETA: Also, thanks for helping me name the article!</p>

